      "title": "Katherine Deves among four NSW upper house candidates revealed by One Nation",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/15/katherine-deves-among-four-nsw-upper-house-candidates-revealed-by-one-nation-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Party’s NSW leader Mike Newman says contenders are ‘people from the real world’ and not ‘career politicians’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The failed federal Liberal candidate Katherine Deves, who campaigned to exclude transgender women from women’s sport, will stand for One Nation at next year’s New South Wales election.</p><p>Deves was among four NSW Legislative Council candidates announced by One Nation’s NSW leader, Mike Newman, on Sunday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/15/katherine-deves-among-four-nsw-upper-house-candidates-revealed-by-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-15T02:13:20"
    },
    {
      "title": "Thunderstorms, giant hail and powerful winds forecast for NSW as wild weather hits east coast",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/15/australia-weather-east-coast-thunderstorms-giant-hail-and-powerful-winds-ettalong-beach-swimmer-lightning-strike",
      "description": "<p>Volatile weather predicted after storms on Saturday, with a man in his 20s struck by lightning while swimming on NSW Central Coast</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Dangerous and severe “supercell” thunderstorms with the potential for giant hail and destructive winds were forecast for parts of New South Wales on Sunday, as volatile weather continued in the eastern states over the weekend.</p><p>Storms dumped heavy rain across large parts of northern and eastern NSW and much of Queensland on Saturday, with strong winds recorded up to 98km/h in Goulburn and rainfall totals of between 30mm and 50mm in the Coffs Harbour area.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/15/australia-weather-east-coast-thunderstorms-giant-hail-and-powerful-winds-ettalong-beach-swimmer-lightning-strike\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-15T01:52:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "David Jones’ future looks grim. Is Myer next?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/15/myer-david-jones-stores-closures-administration",
      "description": "<p>With Myer’s profitability battered and share price languishing near all-time lows, DJs’ slide into administration raises an uncomfortable question</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>When the retailer’s doors slide open, shoppers are greeted by rows of slashed price tags, frantic discounting, and all the other hallmarks of a department store closing down.</p><p>Except this isn’t David Jones, the embattled upmarket retailer that is <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/11/david-jones-store-closures-administration-restructure\">shutting half its 38 stores</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/15/myer-david-jones-stores-closures-administration\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-14T23:00:01"
    },
    {
      "title": "Even Labor MPs are at a loss over the Victorian premier’s ‘tough love’ plan for youth offenders",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/15/victoria-premier-ben-caroll-youth-crime-offenders-plan-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Parliamentarians across factional lines share concerns about policy that legal expert says ‘paints the imprisonment of children as therapeutic’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Until December last year, Meena Singh was Victoria’s commissioner for Aboriginal children and young people, a role in which she advocated for some of the state’s most vulnerable children.</p><p>She had held the role since 2022. In all that time, she says, nobody from the Victorian government had approached her with a proposal like the one the Victorian premier, Ben Carroll, announced last week: a $204m “tough love” plan to send children who commit low- and mid-level offences to secure facilities, including the former Malmsbury youth justice centre, for schooling, drug and alcohol treatment and to learn life skills.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/15/victoria-premier-ben-caroll-youth-crime-offenders-plan-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-14T19:00:53"
    },
    {
      "title": "Art ‘must not be sacrificed on the altar of corporate profit’, Liberal senator says as AI policy debate rages",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/15/art-over-profit-ai-policy-debate-andrew-mclachlan",
      "description": "<p>Andrew McLachlan says he chooses ‘real forests over virtual ones’ as he urges Labor government to consider AI’s impact on artists and environment</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The outspoken Liberal senator Andrew McLachlan has raised the alarm about the approach of his party and the Labor government to AI, saying artists’ copyright must not be “sacrificed” for investment and building new datacentres must not be prioritised above environmental concerns.</p><p>As <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/09/weakening-ai-copyright-law-will-spell-disaster-for-creativity-australia\">Labor considers copyright changes in an AI policy suite</a> including datacentres, online safety, energy resources and economic benefits, the South Australian backbencher added weight to mooted constitutional challenges as to whether watering down copyright law <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/law/2026/oct/31/experts-warn-ai-copyright-changes-could-breach-australian-constitution-and-spark-huge-compensation-rights-case\">would be an illegal acquisition of property</a>.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/15/art-over-profit-ai-policy-debate-andrew-mclachlan\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-14T19:00:52"
    }
